; THE ROUND KEY CONVEYOR  one round key taken off the front of the schedule
; buffer  which is two hundred and forty cells  and the whole buffer slid up to
; meet the next one;
;
; THE NAME CARRIES THE BUFFER LENGTH  as keccak/sponge136 and sponge168 do
; and for the same reason: the length is not an offset  it is the NUMBER OF
; MOVES  so it is different text and not the same text at a different base;
; the other AES key size wants a buffer of its own length  so it has a
; pair of its own;
;
; THIS IS THE OTHER HALF OF THE STORED SCHEDULE DESIGN; its sibling puts a
; word on the tail as the schedule is made  and this takes sixteen bytes off
; the head as the cipher runs; Between them no round key is ever addressed by
; a computed offset  which is the library's conveyor rule and the reason an
; AES_256 cipher is the same text as an AES_128 one with a different count;
;
; A MOVE AND NOT A COPY  in both halves; the round key cells are SPENT by
; AddRoundKey  which exclusive ors the key into the state and empties it  so
; the buffer hands its head over rather than lending it; The entry contract
; below claims those sixteen cells are already clear  which is the cheap
; guard against the copy where a move belonged: a copy into an occupied cell
; ADDS  and the answer is wrong somewhere far away;
;
; TWO HUNDRED AND FORTY MOVES A TURN  sixteen to take the key
; and two hundred and twenty four to close the gap  and a cipher turns it once
; per round; It is the same arithmetic the appending half does from the
; other end  and against a round of AES it is not measurable;
;
; THE TAIL EMPTIES AS THE CONVEYOR RUNS; after the slide the top sixteen
; cells hold nothing  because the slide moved out of them and nothing moved
; in; The exit contract says so  and that is what would catch a slide whose
; count was one word short;
;
; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE and the include's offset resolves them;
;
; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero  which IS the round key cell)
;   @0x000:0x00f  round key{16}  clear on entry  full on exit
;   @0x322:0x411  the schedule buffer{240}  shorter by a round key on exit
;
; ASSERT ptr=+0
; ASSERT zero +0:+15

; ==== the head sixteen bytes become the round key ====
; key bytes 0 to 3
  R802[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]
; key bytes 4 to 7
  R1[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]
; key bytes 8 to 11
  R1[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]
; key bytes 12 to 15
  R1[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]R1[-L802+R802]
; ASSERT ptr=+817

